Fix Hyprland compositor crash when a screencopy client asks for a capture
frame on an output that has just been removed (SIGSEGV in
Screenshare::CScreenshareFrame::transform).

Root cause: CScreenshareSession::monitor() deliberately returns nullptr once
its PHLMONITORREF expires, and every other consumer in ScreenshareFrame.cpp
(done(), share()) null-checks it. CScreenshareFrame::transform() does not --
it dereferences m_session->monitor() straight into ->m_transform. The
ext-image-copy-capture frame constructor calls it unconditionally at the end
of CImageCopyCaptureFrame::CImageCopyCaptureFrame (sendTransform), so any
create_frame request that is already in flight when the output disappears
faults the compositor.

Observed on resume from S3 with an external monitor unplugged while asleep:
aquamarine drops HDMI-A-1 ("Connector HDMI-A-1 disconnected / Disabling
output"), the session's monitorDestroyed listener stops the session and sends
`stopped`, but the client (a Quickshell ScreencopyView lock backdrop built
from a Quickshell.screens model that has not yet observed the wl_output going
away) has already queued create_frame. The protocol requires the compositor to
tolerate requests sent before the client processes `stopped`.

With the guard the frame is still created and simply reports the default
transform; the client's subsequent capture request fails cleanly through the
existing CScreenshareFrame::share() -> ERROR_STOPPED -> sendFailed(STOPPED)
path, so no further change is needed.

Applies to Hyprland v0.56.0 and v0.56.1 (the deref is byte-identical in both;
nothing in the v0.56.0..v0.56.1 diff touches this file).

Upstream: the crash site no longer exists on main -- 901881c9 "render: always
render in normal transform (#15714)" (2026-08-04) reduced transform() to
`return WL_OUTPUT_TRANSFORM_NORMAL;` as a side effect of a rendering refactor,
not as a crash fix. That commit is NOT on the 0.56.x release branch, so every
shipped 0.56.x is still vulnerable and this patch is the backport. It does not
apply to main (the context is gone); drop it when moving past 0.56.x.

See docs/hyprland-screencopy-dead-output-crash for the full analysis.
---
diff --git a/src/managers/screenshare/ScreenshareFrame.cpp b/src/managers/screenshare/ScreenshareFrame.cpp
--- a/src/managers/screenshare/ScreenshareFrame.cpp
+++ b/src/managers/screenshare/ScreenshareFrame.cpp
@@ -508,9 +508,19 @@ Vector2D CScreenshareFrame::bufferSize() const {
 }

 wl_output_transform CScreenshareFrame::transform() const {
+    if UNLIKELY (m_session.expired())
+        return WL_OUTPUT_TRANSFORM_NORMAL;
+
     switch (m_session->m_type) {
         case SHARE_REGION:
-        case SHARE_MONITOR: return m_session->monitor()->m_transform;
+        case SHARE_MONITOR: {
+            // The shared monitor can be gone by the time a client asks for the
+            // frame's transform: CScreenshareSession::monitor() returns nullptr
+            // once m_monitor expires, and dereferencing it faults. done() and
+            // share() already null-check it, this path did not.
+            const auto MON = m_session->monitor();
+            return MON ? MON->m_transform : WL_OUTPUT_TRANSFORM_NORMAL;
+        }
         default:
         case SHARE_WINDOW: return WL_OUTPUT_TRANSFORM_NORMAL;
     }
